# A task file written by copying another and edited everywhere but the id. Two
# tasks keyed the same are one claim covering two pieces of work, which is the
# mistake this catches — and it is caught by the naming rule, because two files
# cannot both be the file named for M1-01.
run available
exit 3
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stderr
	tasks.sh: tasks/M1-02.md: frontmatter says id M1-01, and a task file is named for the id it carries
